! jb_af1c F217-XC "TEST UNCHANGED REGS", p.163 (octal
! 021201.00-021212.40, the block's own exit "B,$+1.0").  Continues
! fp_arith_f217xb.strap and finishes F217-X.
!
! p.94: R/'s writeback is DIVIDE's -- "The quotient exponent and
! fraction replace accumulator bits 0-59.  Accumulator bits 60-127
! remain unchanged" -- so this fills L, R and the sign byte with ones,
! does an R/, and demands the right word and the sign byte's other
! seven bits come back ones.  Bit 4 is skipped, being the quotient
! sign.
!
! IT CANNOT DISCRIMINATE WHERE THE FLAG BITS COME FROM, which is worth
! recording because R/ is the one operation where the question has two
! plausible answers.  The arm takes SB 5-7 from the ACCUMULATOR, since
! for R/ the result's own flags come from the dividend -- the storage
! operand -- and the accumulator's are what should survive.  But here
! the sign byte is filled with ones (flags 7) and the dividend is FPK1
! (flags 7), so both readings write 111 and XC passes either way.
!
! The divisor is the accumulator, all ones, whose fraction is
! ffffffffffff -- a real division, not a suppressed one.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes: SERS (octal 1304) -> FAIL halt,
! -- SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch.
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pool p.176) --
        SLC, (8)22006.0
FPK1    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777777777777777777777

        SLC, (8)21201.0
F217XC  C1111(BU,64), FPK1, 64               ! left word <- all ones
        C1111(BU,64), FPK1                   ! right word <- all ones
        CM1111(BU,8), $SB                    ! sign byte <- all ones
        R/(U), FPK1
        CT1010(BU,64), FPK1                  ! does R remain +1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1100(BU,4), $SB                    ! does SB 0-3 remain +1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        CT1100(BU,3), $SB+.5                 ! does SB 5-7 remain +1 s
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                               ! 021212.40: the block's exit "B,$+1.0"
        END, F217XC
